      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly provide a general definition of “temporal stability” as “the extent to which a psychological measure or trait shows similar results when assessed again over time.” It only reports that a specific study assessed test–retest reliability/stability coefficients for a particular instrument (RPBS).",
        "The definition’s statement that temporal stability “refers to consistency across repeated time points” is not stated as a definition in the packet; the packet only describes that the RPBS was measured at three time points and that test–retest reliability/stability coefficients were evaluated.",
